From 08fb6a138242a822af7725365a01f1f5e07ee260 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GibaxLeGrand <48137851+GibaxLeGrand@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 22:10:18 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Runner: "LEVEL UP!!" for this machine's seat

The level is worked out for every racer on every machine (0x80431CD0, called from the HUD's code):
measured by giving racer 0 forty rings on all runners at one paused frame, level 3 everywhere and no
divergence. Its display task (0x804205C4) is made for every racer alike and, in its first state, goes
on to the 1P drawing whenever the player count is 1: every racer's level change showed on every screen
(seen: Sonic's "LEVEL UP!!" over Shadow's and Tails's HUD). During the race the task's racer index is
compared with the seat (0x8042065C, 0x80420660) and the other racers' tasks go to their end (state 1,
0x80420678) instead of the multi-screen drawing: the task, its sound and bookkeeping stay the same
everywhere; only its table entry (a display pointer, outside the racers' checksum) is cleared sooner.
Measured on the same race: "LEVEL UP!!" on Sonic's screen alone, Shadow's and Tails's HUD whole; 36
identical checksums.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/runtime/srnp_racers.cpp | 21 +++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/runtime/srnp_racers.cpp b/src/runtime/srnp_racers.cpp
index 30d1bb7..4d00d22 100644
--- a/src/runtime/srnp_racers.cpp
+++ b/src/runtime/srnp_racers.cpp
@@ -638,6 +638,26 @@ SeatDisplay s_tricks{
       return i == 0 ? 0x28000000u | static_cast<std::uint32_t>(seat + 1) : 0x40820790u;
     }};
 
+// "LEVEL UP!!" (and the level down): the level is worked out for every racer on every machine
+// (0x80431CD0; measured on 2026-11-25: 40 rings given to racer 0 on all runners, level 3 everywhere,
+// no divergence), and its display task (0x804205C4) is made for every racer alike, kept at
+// 0x80612984[index]; in its first state (0x80420638) the task goes on to the 1P drawing (state 3) when the
+// player count is 1, so every racer's level change showed on every screen. Written: lbz r0, 0x1029(r19)
+// (the task's racer index); cmplwi r0, <seat>; and the other racers' tasks go to state 1 (their end:
+// the table entry cleared, the task deleted) instead of 5. The task, its sound and its bookkeeping stay
+// the same everywhere; only that table entry (a display task's pointer, outside the racers' checksum,
+// RacersHash) is cleared sooner on the other machines.
+SeatDisplay s_level_up{
+    "level up",
+    {{0x8042065C, 0x8003B8C8},   // lwz r0, -0x4738(r3) (the player count)
+     {0x80420660, 0x28000001},   // cmplwi r0, 1
+     {0x80420678, 0x38000005}},  // li r0, 5
+    3,
+    [](std::size_t i, int seat) {
+      constexpr std::uint32_t words[] = {0x88131029u, 0x28000000u, 0x38000001u};
+      return i == 1 ? words[1] | static_cast<std::uint32_t>(seat) : words[i];
+    }};
+
 void PatchSeatDisplay(SeatDisplay& d, int seat)
 {
   static const bool off = [] {
@@ -676,6 +696,7 @@ void PatchSeatDisplays(int seat)
 {
   PatchSeatDisplay(s_item_boxes, seat);
   PatchSeatDisplay(s_tricks, seat);
+  PatchSeatDisplay(s_level_up, seat);
 }
 
 // SRNP_PATCH=<address>=<word>,... (hexadecimal): code words written for the race, for experiments
